  -> h93's caveat ('moves BOTH gravity laws equally') is wrong for the three deep-MOND clusters: the law is nearly r-independent
     there.  Size of the slip: a 10% r_h error shifts the Newton-vs-law differential by ~4%.  Immaterial to every verdict.

