  intrinsic sigma = Newton (Wolf, Upsilon 1.6): Pal 3 0.74, Pal 4 1.00, Pal 14 0.60 km/s
  CFG334 frozen rule: EXPLAIN if P(Pal 3) >= 0.05 at (0.75, e 1.0, f 0.3); PLAUSIBLE if only at f 0.5 / e 1.5.
  -> unclipped (as CFG334 ran it) the primary P reproduces (~0.26). With a standard 3-sigma clip the primary falls to ~0.045:
     the verdict would read PLAUSIBLE, not EXPLAIN.  Whether Baumgardt's 1.70 was clipped/membership-filtered is NOT on disk.
  -> joint test (same binary population in all three sparse clusters, Newton intrinsic): Fisher p >= ~0.1 at f 0.3 --
     a binary population big enough for Pal 3 leaves Pal 4 / Pal 14 low-ish but not inconsistent.  Not a refutation.
